      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "Last night, an AS350 crew acquired a lights-out Yola vessel, off the coast of Aguada, Puerto Rico. 2 Michel O. Maceda Marine Unit CIV crews and a UH-60 launched to intercept.  Once on scene the CIV crews and UH-60 attempted to stop the vessel which refused to heave to. Marine Interdiction Agents deployed two marine warning shots in conjunction with the Small Boat Interdiction Program which prompted the vessel to stop without further  incident. 8 illegal aliens were apprehended, 3 Venezuelan, 1 Colombian, and 4 Dominican nationals. The subjects were transferred to the United States Border Patrol for further processing.  #ProtectingAmerica #BorderSecurity",
      "text_resolved": "Last night, an AS350 crew acquired a lights-out Yola vessel, off the coast of Aguada, Puerto Rico. 2 Michel O. Maceda Marine Unit CIV crews and a UH-60 launched to intercept.  Once on scene the CIV crews and UH-60 attempted to stop the vessel which refused to heave to. Marine Interdiction Agents deployed two marine warning shots in conjunction with the Small Boat Interdiction Program which prompted the vessel to stop without further  incident. 8 illegal aliens were apprehended, 3 Venezuelan, 1 Colombian, and 4 Dominican nationals. The subjects were transferred to the United States Border Patrol for further processing.  #ProtectingAmerica #BorderSecurity",
